# Orchestrator config

Copy this file to `.agent-workspace/config.md` and edit it for your project.
`config.md` is gitignored; this `.example` is the committed template.

## Target repos

Every repo the orchestrator may work on. Add one block per repo. The number of
repos is just the length of this list — one repo or N repos is the same code
path to the pipeline.

`test` is optional: a bounded command that runs the repo's test suite and exits
non-zero on failure (e.g. `npm test`, `pytest`). When present, the implementer
runs it to verify before opening/updating a PR, and the reviewer may run it to
confirm the suite is green. Omit it if the repo has no test suite.

```yaml
repos:
  - slug: example-api
    path: /absolute/path/to/example-api
    test: npm test
  - slug: example-web
    path: /absolute/path/to/example-web
    test: npm test
```

## Tracker

Where tasks come from. One of `github`, `gitlab`, or `none`.

- `github` / `gitlab`: the orchestrator reads the task from an issue/ticket.
- `none`: the orchestrator reads the task from
  `.agent-workspace/feature-request.md`.

```yaml
tracker: none
```

## Conventions

```yaml
branch_convention: "feat/<task>-<repo-slug>"
base_branch: main
```
